                <pb facs="0659" n="575" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg575"/>

                <head>No. 300.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Jackson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-03-08"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 8,
                        1886</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 139.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 158 of the 23d
                    ultimo showing that the Mexican Government is collecting all possible
                    information relative to the unfortunate conflict near Nacori, January 10, 1886,
                    by which Capt. Emmet Crawford lost his life.</p>
                <p>A copy of your dispatch has been communicated to the Secretary of War.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
